<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - Air NZ entry raises Australia competition - BA.</title>
<headline>RTRS - Air NZ entry raises Australia competition - BA.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc chairman Sir Colin Marshall said on Monday that the entry of Air New Zealand Ltd into the Australian domestic market in alliance with Ansett Australia Ltd would obviously intensify competition with Qantas Airways Ltd.</p>
<p>Marshall said BA, which owns 25 percent of Qantas, was however very happy with Qantas' performance and was confident it could withstand the increased competition.</p>
</text>
